---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---
<Base
  title="LightPhotos Blogs"
  desc="Write-ups on why LightPhotos exists and how it's built."
  active="blogs"
>
  <main class="lp-page lp-page--wide">
    <section class="lp-hero lp-hero-compact">
      <div class="lp-glow"></div>
      <h1 class="lp-wordmark">Blogs</h1>
    </section>

    <ul class="lp-post-list">
      <li>
        <a class="lp-post-card" href="/blogs/my-plan.html">
          <div class="lp-post-cover">
            <img src="/blog-covers/my-plan.webp" alt="" width="1200" height="675" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" />
          </div>
          <div class="lp-post-content">
            <h2>My plan, and what's not in it</h2>
            <p class="lp-post-meta">
              <time datetime="2026-09-20">Sep 20, 2026</time>
              <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
              <span>6 min read</span>
            </p>
            <p class="lp-post-blurb">Where LightPhotos is going—and what it will never become.</p>
          </div>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="lp-post-card" href="/blogs/measuring-a-gui-app.html">
          <div class="lp-post-cover">
            <img src="/blog-covers/measuring-a-gui-app.webp" alt="" width="1200" height="675" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </div>
          <div class="lp-post-content">
            <h2>Measuring a GUI app without lying to yourself</h2>
            <p class="lp-post-meta">
              <time datetime="2026-09-15">Sep 15, 2026</time>
              <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
              <span>5 min read</span>
            </p>
            <p class="lp-post-blurb">A repeatable way to measure a GUI app without guessing.</p>
          </div>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="lp-post-card" href="/blogs/never-load-the-whole-folder.html">
          <div class="lp-post-cover">
            <img src="/blog-covers/never-load-the-whole-folder.webp" alt="" width="1200" height="675" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </div>
          <div class="lp-post-content">
            <h2>Never load the whole folder</h2>
            <p class="lp-post-meta">
              <time datetime="2026-09-01">Sep 1, 2026</time>
              <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
              <span>5 min read</span>
            </p>
            <p class="lp-post-blurb">Why the first version of a photo browser ran out of memory.</p>
          </div>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="lp-post-card" href="/blogs/six-queues-and-a-reserved-worker.html">
          <div class="lp-post-cover">
            <img src="/blog-covers/six-queues-and-a-reserved-worker.webp" alt="" width="1200" height="675" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </div>
          <div class="lp-post-content">
            <h2>Six queues and a reserved worker</h2>
            <p class="lp-post-meta">
              <time datetime="2026-08-20">Aug 20, 2026</time>
              <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
              <span>5 min read</span>
            </p>
            <p class="lp-post-blurb">How background decoding stays responsive under pressure.</p>
          </div>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="lp-post-card" href="/blogs/where-your-data-lives.html">
          <div class="lp-post-cover">
            <img src="/blog-covers/where-your-data-lives.webp" alt="" width="1200" height="675" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </div>
          <div class="lp-post-content">
            <h2>Your data lives where you are allowed to write</h2>
            <p class="lp-post-meta">
              <time datetime="2026-08-10">Aug 10, 2026</time>
              <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
              <span>4 min read</span>
            </p>
            <p class="lp-post-blurb">Why photos, edits, and metadata stay in ordinary folders.</p>
          </div>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="lp-post-card" href="/blogs/what-imageio-gives-you-free.html">
          <div class="lp-post-cover">
            <img src="/blog-covers/what-imageio-gives-you-free.webp" alt="" width="1200" height="675" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </div>
          <div class="lp-post-content">
            <h2>What ImageIO gives you free, and what it costs to leave</h2>
            <p class="lp-post-meta">
              <time datetime="2026-07-20">Jul 20, 2026</time>
              <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
              <span>4 min read</span>
            </p>
            <p class="lp-post-blurb">What ImageIO gives you—and what portability costs.</p>
          </div>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="lp-post-card" href="/blogs/how-a-photo-gets-on-screen.html">
          <div class="lp-post-cover">
            <img src="/blog-covers/how-a-photo-gets-on-screen.webp" alt="" width="1200" height="675" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </div>
          <div class="lp-post-content">
            <h2>How a photo gets on screen</h2>
            <p class="lp-post-meta">
              <time datetime="2026-07-08">Jul 8, 2026</time>
              <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
              <span>6 min read</span>
            </p>
            <p class="lp-post-blurb">The path from a raw file to pixels on your display.</p>
          </div>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="lp-post-card" href="/blogs/learning-rust-while-the-agents-write-it.html">
          <div class="lp-post-cover">
            <img src="/blog-covers/learning-rust-while-the-agents-write-it.webp" alt="" width="1200" height="675" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </div>
          <div class="lp-post-content">
            <h2>Learning Rust while the agents write it</h2>
            <p class="lp-post-meta">
              <time datetime="2026-07-02">Jul 2, 2026</time>
              <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
              <span>8 min read</span>
            </p>
            <p class="lp-post-blurb">A practical loop for learning while agents write the code.</p>
          </div>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="lp-post-card" href="/blogs/why-rust.html">
          <div class="lp-post-cover">
            <img src="/blog-covers/why-rust.webp" alt="" width="1200" height="675" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </div>
          <div class="lp-post-content">
            <h2>Why Rust</h2>
            <p class="lp-post-meta">
              <time datetime="2026-06-28">Jun 28, 2026</time>
              <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
              <span>6 min read</span>
            </p>
            <p class="lp-post-blurb">The architecture decision behind LightPhotos.</p>
          </div>
        </a>
      </li>
      <li>
        <a class="lp-post-card" href="/blogs/why-i-started-lightphotos.html">
          <div class="lp-post-cover">
            <img src="/blog-covers/why-i-started-lightphotos.webp" alt="" width="1200" height="675" loading="lazy" decoding="async" />
          </div>
          <div class="lp-post-content">
            <h2>Why I started LightPhotos</h2>
            <p class="lp-post-meta">
              <time datetime="2026-06-23">Jun 23, 2026</time>
              <span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
              <span>5 min read</span>
            </p>
            <p class="lp-post-blurb">The lost photo library that started a small photo editor.</p>
          </div>
        </a>
      </li>
    </ul>
  </main>
</Base>
